[{:db/id "q-33627/selection/0c140b004b67c6e779fb625f006419a4576f5eed9107b2476bc8b762374f10ae" :answer/id #uuid "6d375a58-62fb-539a-92f2-8e92d0b5a2e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1+t}⟨-1,\\,{t}^{2},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33627/selection/e7847d759da4e6ffd73ff10e72652dc537deaf373d8005c26191f213b07e87d0" :answer/id #uuid "3cb948c3-0083-5b8d-b43f-baa6ad1480cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1+{t}^{2}}⟨-1,\\,{t}^{2},\\,2t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33627/selection/4cf7a1d43721b5d040ac376e2cc596df62d636cbe8a54b7888cd8ce67af30e1a" :answer/id #uuid "b9082141-046c-5b86-82a5-3e3e13f010a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1+t}⟨1,\\,{t}^{2},\\,\\sqrt{2}t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33627/selection/e8ee1535a16d89f49803e4edf987ae9e2445f31d382ff08d1e91f93ab1ba346c" :answer/id #uuid "2c22f924-bf8d-5b04-b856-bc86dbeec79f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1+{t}^{2}}⟨-1,\\,{t}^{2},\\,\\sqrt{2}{t}^{2}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33627/selection/f9bf39ade4828470c78d0009e8661898ea2521e3d485bdba565b7cd193fac260" :answer/id #uuid "34285464-2898-547c-9912-ce74c45038c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1+{t}^{2}}⟨-1,\\,{t}^{2},\\,\\sqrt{2}t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33627/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "83a44c6a-89ca-5b14-8d82-5d17869f5ec5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-33627/selection/f9bf39ade4828470c78d0009e8661898ea2521e3d485bdba565b7cd193fac260" :answer-field/choices ["q-33627/selection/0c140b004b67c6e779fb625f006419a4576f5eed9107b2476bc8b762374f10ae" "q-33627/selection/e7847d759da4e6ffd73ff10e72652dc537deaf373d8005c26191f213b07e87d0" "q-33627/selection/4cf7a1d43721b5d040ac376e2cc596df62d636cbe8a54b7888cd8ce67af30e1a" "q-33627/selection/e8ee1535a16d89f49803e4edf987ae9e2445f31d382ff08d1e91f93ab1ba346c" "q-33627/selection/f9bf39ade4828470c78d0009e8661898ea2521e3d485bdba565b7cd193fac260"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-33627" :question/id #uuid "999eae56-9014-5e14-ac70-9c3dd9daada7" :question/math-academy-id "q-33627" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the unit tangent vector to the curve\n $r(t)=⟨\\frac{1}{t},\\,t,\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t⟩$ at an arbitrary point where $t\\in (0,\\infty )?$" :question/worked-solution "For a curve $r(t)=⟨x(t),\\,y(t),\\,z(t)⟩$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $r(t):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\sqrt{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,1,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{t}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}})}^{2}+(1)^{2}+{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}}+1+\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1+{t}^{4}+2{t}^{2}}{{t}^{4}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{(1+{t}^{2})^{2}}{{t}^{4}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+{t}^{2}}{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n Finally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}}{1+{t}^{2}}⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,1,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{t}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+{t}^{2}}⟨-1,\\,{t}^{2},\\,\\sqrt{2}t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-33627/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c400d85b-94d5-5fd2-98b4-472ab43c5be4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-33627"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-74893/selection/1a8a1000db5e2b2fc16e587ce60a7830e83d67b3995166347cc76e4c7aa23485" :answer/id #uuid "acdbdcd9-8f55-5bd0-9060-7101fd6ff0e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{({t}^{2}-4)}(4t\\,i+({t}^{2}+4)\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74893/selection/f478e3e3387e90dd1771dd721541d0aae22cb0d92c014843849a2eb45446c27b" :answer/id #uuid "9b4d5458-d07e-524a-8bf3-62368dcfcf2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1})}(t\\,i+(2{t}^{2}-4)\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74893/selection/4fffada871b49294183f50f6ac44955a117c6f6c9c0ace4096dd10867d4b1970" :answer/id #uuid "717f5d41-905a-5fc9-89be-36ed4fb365bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{({t}^{2}+4)}(4t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,i+({t}^{2}-\\frac{4}{{t}^{2}})\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74893/selection/4cc7c30dcb17c6a4d69a89e0cbb375a7be03c648b657feb3366f0d24f9878ac4" :answer/id #uuid "9b18c319-5aef-5ec8-b131-75592638d86a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{t}{({t}^{2}+4)}({t}^{2}\\,i+(2t-4)\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74893/selection/7b994196c3b0587508b1e45c44c5eda8e75ca1091343de04175be1aa3e097f6c" :answer/id #uuid "82c21578-9535-5e45-a036-8833094c10de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{({t}^{2}+4)}(4t\\,i+({t}^{2}-4)\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74893/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e4fa452a-254e-5f1a-a4d1-759b2087e477" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74893/selection/7b994196c3b0587508b1e45c44c5eda8e75ca1091343de04175be1aa3e097f6c" :answer-field/choices ["q-74893/selection/1a8a1000db5e2b2fc16e587ce60a7830e83d67b3995166347cc76e4c7aa23485" "q-74893/selection/f478e3e3387e90dd1771dd721541d0aae22cb0d92c014843849a2eb45446c27b" "q-74893/selection/4fffada871b49294183f50f6ac44955a117c6f6c9c0ace4096dd10867d4b1970" "q-74893/selection/4cc7c30dcb17c6a4d69a89e0cbb375a7be03c648b657feb3366f0d24f9878ac4" "q-74893/selection/7b994196c3b0587508b1e45c44c5eda8e75ca1091343de04175be1aa3e097f6c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74893" :question/id #uuid "a16e85af-77b2-5931-96dd-f6f496c8bbed" :question/math-academy-id "q-74893" :question/problem "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=4\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,i+(t+\\frac{4}{t})\\,j$ at an arbitrary point where $t\\in (0,\\infty ).$" :question/worked-solution "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+\\frac{4}{t})\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{t}\\,i+(1-\\frac{4}{{t}^{2}})\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{4}{t})}^{2}+{(1-\\frac{4}{{t}^{2}})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{16}{{t}^{2}}+{(1-\\frac{8}{{t}^{2}}+\\frac{16}{{t}^{4}})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{8}{{t}^{2}}+\\frac{16}{{t}^{4}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}}({t}^{4}+8{t}^{2}+16)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}}{({t}^{2}+4)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{({t}^{2}+4)}{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}}{({t}^{2}+4)}(\\frac{4}{t}\\,i+(1-\\frac{4}{{t}^{2}})\\,j) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{({t}^{2}+4)}(4t\\,i+({t}^{2}-4)\\,j)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-74893/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c400d85b-94d5-5fd2-98b4-472ab43c5be4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74893"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-74891/selection/bd53baf2f7e9414b5355a899f769c55ff50eeb1bf869ab0ef8064ed5aa65a975" :answer/id #uuid "61333e51-89ac-5ac3-95b9-4379fc49262a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74891/selection/f331be36f1eeb1a161a2f7c4db68f32efe65ac7d16b2e18b60d42d1867b3079d" :answer/id #uuid "6ae3283f-aa95-5d93-b82f-728b188465b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74891/selection/be847164e0c99ec16a9bc6485614058cb0186ee5ba79ece38d884c52dfc20b9c" :answer/id #uuid "af23b667-f69d-55b4-afea-0e92ecea476a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74891/selection/9e9572615c2cf7afa2fa44a6493d22ff020e153c64ad1a6f5b00348c5a3b19f3" :answer/id #uuid "30f111d3-2662-5736-b1a3-f8cc718ccd1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74891/selection/6ae763d911cd6e55d5bca63eed3ebbbae73c8f50d3dbc1e7e4eaa56c9d15eb58" :answer/id #uuid "3885fe27-60c8-5751-a3b7-74c6ddd043ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74891/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bd4155f4-c448-57f4-b061-424d2ffa0455" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74891/selection/be847164e0c99ec16a9bc6485614058cb0186ee5ba79ece38d884c52dfc20b9c" :answer-field/choices ["q-74891/selection/bd53baf2f7e9414b5355a899f769c55ff50eeb1bf869ab0ef8064ed5aa65a975" "q-74891/selection/f331be36f1eeb1a161a2f7c4db68f32efe65ac7d16b2e18b60d42d1867b3079d" "q-74891/selection/be847164e0c99ec16a9bc6485614058cb0186ee5ba79ece38d884c52dfc20b9c" "q-74891/selection/9e9572615c2cf7afa2fa44a6493d22ff020e153c64ad1a6f5b00348c5a3b19f3" "q-74891/selection/6ae763d911cd6e55d5bca63eed3ebbbae73c8f50d3dbc1e7e4eaa56c9d15eb58"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74891" :question/id #uuid "e2939faf-302b-5f44-aabb-06f4cf0b6acc" :question/math-academy-id "q-74891" :question/problem "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,j$ at an arbitrary point where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" :question/worked-solution "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)\\,j \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)^{2}+(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{sin}^{2}⁡2t+4{cos}^{2}⁡2t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({sin}^{2}⁡2t+{cos}^{2}⁡2t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-74891/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c400d85b-94d5-5fd2-98b4-472ab43c5be4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74891"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127212/selection/38541e6e69e86feef741406a8ce53c8eae8f4da8cfaa043025eb171ed721a995" :answer/id #uuid "407da90f-b369-51bd-a5b2-77bb16346dda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127212/selection/272908ebe60461d6968fe5e5713da93f2c1e1aad1aa89edca51684c1d9e778d8" :answer/id #uuid "3bd315ff-a891-5962-b016-bce1bc0ae5b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127212/selection/ae84f388898f9cc998d974ae003cf2e0b84daa1a8f5cd0e0f6ba15cd996c21a1" :answer/id #uuid "99652878-ed07-5647-804d-89feea920b63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127212/selection/f02a22b2fa638cf7c7a5b20ff0e69748610f911db285b2dbd788940a5688228c" :answer/id #uuid "7c79c005-d22b-5274-a96a-d4c4b9a22a37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127212/selection/cf4f6796f63b8be3c03e65b739aa55bb0921e64f1cbfd0aefbe055af986417ee" :answer/id #uuid "49dc7313-407a-5c7b-9421-1dd3133758bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127212/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "65abc716-e155-5a63-b11d-e021e06d210f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127212/selection/272908ebe60461d6968fe5e5713da93f2c1e1aad1aa89edca51684c1d9e778d8" :answer-field/choices ["q-127212/selection/38541e6e69e86feef741406a8ce53c8eae8f4da8cfaa043025eb171ed721a995" "q-127212/selection/272908ebe60461d6968fe5e5713da93f2c1e1aad1aa89edca51684c1d9e778d8" "q-127212/selection/ae84f388898f9cc998d974ae003cf2e0b84daa1a8f5cd0e0f6ba15cd996c21a1" "q-127212/selection/f02a22b2fa638cf7c7a5b20ff0e69748610f911db285b2dbd788940a5688228c" "q-127212/selection/cf4f6796f63b8be3c03e65b739aa55bb0921e64f1cbfd0aefbe055af986417ee"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127212" :question/id #uuid "f99f8518-2669-5410-a726-3aa328247590" :question/math-academy-id "q-127212" :question/problem "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩$ at an arbitrary point where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" :question/worked-solution "For a curve $r(t)=⟨x(t),\\,y(t)⟩$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+9{sin}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-127212/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c400d85b-94d5-5fd2-98b4-472ab43c5be4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127212"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127213/selection/6614e10a377f7f4e883efbed28c77264395ab345081e6e21b25fe93ec5de9da0" :answer/id #uuid "d8e669c5-474c-54ec-9b1a-57663e4d586d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1+4t}(i-\\sqrt{t}\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127213/selection/0c7402e609f1290c3f732cae891d7f33cb8c428fc2edcec68c4aa23509dcbf8b" :answer/id #uuid "e56f8f54-bfa8-5ed9-80d3-b0bbc21bbeda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4t}}(i-\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127213/selection/51ae5bd600a080bea94b38f3b26fdd56845fa4ff619c40e0d5046887564a8ec0" :answer/id #uuid "db57f7ca-962f-50e6-a503-551e18b29a64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4t}}(\\sqrt{t}\\,i-2t\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127213/selection/787726a845344be80293b9e1cfc2bb6f8be2f90c2e03d6d038920aec65a0b449" :answer/id #uuid "4ea4ea58-e74e-5dcb-b2a7-6271320606bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1+4t}(3i+2\\sqrt{t}\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127213/selection/4e949da918b22608d9322f4a02a0e74a09acab0be550ee030aae44566a848861" :answer/id #uuid "d625ce53-3f65-5483-bff7-7c35b855dfb3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4t}}(i-2\\sqrt{t}\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127213/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "63eb97a8-40b9-53b8-a175-099d9f9a01c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127213/selection/4e949da918b22608d9322f4a02a0e74a09acab0be550ee030aae44566a848861" :answer-field/choices ["q-127213/selection/6614e10a377f7f4e883efbed28c77264395ab345081e6e21b25fe93ec5de9da0" "q-127213/selection/0c7402e609f1290c3f732cae891d7f33cb8c428fc2edcec68c4aa23509dcbf8b" "q-127213/selection/51ae5bd600a080bea94b38f3b26fdd56845fa4ff619c40e0d5046887564a8ec0" "q-127213/selection/787726a845344be80293b9e1cfc2bb6f8be2f90c2e03d6d038920aec65a0b449" "q-127213/selection/4e949da918b22608d9322f4a02a0e74a09acab0be550ee030aae44566a848861"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127213" :question/id #uuid "1cfc1910-4d17-5781-a2d7-34d0eb0a5a61" :question/math-academy-id "q-127213" :question/problem "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=\\sqrt{t}\\,i+(2-t)\\,j$ at an arbitrary point where $t\\in (0,\\infty ).$" :question/worked-solution "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2-t)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\,i-\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}})}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4t}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1+4t}{4t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{1+4t}}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{t}}{\\sqrt{1+4t}}(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}i-\\,j) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4t}}(i-2\\sqrt{t}\\,j)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-127213/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c400d85b-94d5-5fd2-98b4-472ab43c5be4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127213"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-33655/selection/59855c86f5d05627b93452c5f7f596e6c2edb3ceabb18fbf0dc1efe7db1f3952" :answer/id #uuid "dcb9aca5-f9a6-5f6a-9719-7d7f257828c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33655/selection/46f9a41a21457a80d3e8174d1142185ec30f26221d00344301358e2e68dccb6f" :answer/id #uuid "7a526db6-2810-5253-921f-d0e056df39de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33655/selection/207f3c4f6d25b37441ab09fc6da896c1bb533e888fc3a797ef164dc6ecee7572" :answer/id #uuid "20e24c61-3ca5-5059-959b-69294f045281" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33655/selection/7547e2750b2ff7fd3169465c192cdce299db86a64fbb706461fcae50c7bfe955" :answer/id #uuid "775af2b0-5896-596a-ac26-3a36e7e6ea2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33655/selection/840e3c28964e6b8d08a5447db6d3a44d9f40b1544aee267792b9bac2b29969ae" :answer/id #uuid "1d7f4363-8319-5a60-8ae9-e88f9bbe6f29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}},\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}},\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33655/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a57e84c6-5d42-5f67-9ff0-52b8d0eadf8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-33655/selection/7547e2750b2ff7fd3169465c192cdce299db86a64fbb706461fcae50c7bfe955" :answer-field/choices ["q-33655/selection/59855c86f5d05627b93452c5f7f596e6c2edb3ceabb18fbf0dc1efe7db1f3952" "q-33655/selection/46f9a41a21457a80d3e8174d1142185ec30f26221d00344301358e2e68dccb6f" "q-33655/selection/207f3c4f6d25b37441ab09fc6da896c1bb533e888fc3a797ef164dc6ecee7572" "q-33655/selection/7547e2750b2ff7fd3169465c192cdce299db86a64fbb706461fcae50c7bfe955" "q-33655/selection/840e3c28964e6b8d08a5447db6d3a44d9f40b1544aee267792b9bac2b29969ae"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-33655" :question/id #uuid "c506b7f3-325f-50a6-8547-719d5dedc2ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-33655" :question/problem "What is the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{4},\\,{t}^{2},\\,4t⟩$ at the point $P(1,1,4)?$" :question/worked-solution "For a curve $r(t)=⟨x(t),y(t),z(t)⟩$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(1,1,4)$ on the given curve. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,4⟩ \\\\ ⟨{t}^{4},\\,{t}^{2},\\,4t⟩ & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the respective components gives the system\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}{t}^{4}=1 \\\\ {t}^{2}=1 \\\\ 4t=4.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equality, we get $t=1.$ This value satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, the point $P(1,1,4)$ is at the tip of $r(1).$  \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4{t}^{3},\\,2t,\\,4⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(1) & =⟨4(1)^{3},\\,2(1),\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,2,\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(1)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at $P(1,1,4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(1)}{‖{r}^{′}(1)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}⟨4,\\,2,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-33655/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ff1822c-afad-54f8-aa36-7e0de79d9d04"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-33655"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127221/selection/02b8c6a43d15698dc9a7b1d5c3b14d6e989cbec17c84b7800cc468c83502a240" :answer/id #uuid "2f321c1a-1787-597f-93b3-bdabbb670efd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4},-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127221/selection/444e61baebeeed9caa78a53f40455ef3f7bdbbad1e341810bd947851120161a5" :answer/id #uuid "ac12147b-057b-5062-a679-12c246430abc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{3}{4},\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127221/selection/1243739bf8ce07abc6468afd7f3a3674560a4147f2e3cb506d63b9cfc04a71da" :answer/id #uuid "19183afe-c2ac-5a80-8a30-718cb68bbbda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3}{4},\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4},\\frac{1}{2}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127221/selection/fee472c757cfd73b54be7a8929e5eadeea880e5b71d8c37f6f6357f5f1e5ca21" :answer/id #uuid "3976cdaf-ca61-59d7-aee5-ea4bb79457f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨3,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},4⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127221/selection/8e7b914c0bfcc60a9cc1c910d45dbb2427d7e3e52f001f214681e6c0e8a6ab7e" :answer/id #uuid "50af0f56-ce43-53d4-9721-ac6b266df3cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{1}{4}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127221/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "34a76364-be75-535c-bb76-2bae0e2e10b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127221/selection/1243739bf8ce07abc6468afd7f3a3674560a4147f2e3cb506d63b9cfc04a71da" :answer-field/choices ["q-127221/selection/02b8c6a43d15698dc9a7b1d5c3b14d6e989cbec17c84b7800cc468c83502a240" "q-127221/selection/444e61baebeeed9caa78a53f40455ef3f7bdbbad1e341810bd947851120161a5" "q-127221/selection/1243739bf8ce07abc6468afd7f3a3674560a4147f2e3cb506d63b9cfc04a71da" "q-127221/selection/fee472c757cfd73b54be7a8929e5eadeea880e5b71d8c37f6f6357f5f1e5ca21" "q-127221/selection/8e7b914c0bfcc60a9cc1c910d45dbb2427d7e3e52f001f214681e6c0e8a6ab7e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127221" :question/id #uuid "3540ef43-cb67-51c1-8423-cebf06f99cf4" :question/math-academy-id "q-127221" :question/problem "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=⟨-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$ at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a curve $r(t)=⟨x(t),y(t),z(t)⟩$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =⟨\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3})‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}^{2}+(1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}+\\frac{3}{4}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3})$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3})}{‖{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3})‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3}{4},\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4},\\frac{1}{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-127221/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ff1822c-afad-54f8-aa36-7e0de79d9d04"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127221"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-33136/selection/e8d6feaa001eb3c9330fa1ba584495e0468f420576d60f79541ab81caf1ae026" :answer/id #uuid "72d9a5aa-94cf-501a-944c-9714c3e9745d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{7}},\\,0,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{7}}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33136/selection/f91e2a7ff49a9f08d8794e2ce1312cf01e9f082d710055202362908d714e9a41" :answer/id #uuid "6f6cdb16-97a3-5d3d-9c7f-3add56eab9cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,0,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33136/selection/a7aad54674d1bdc909be7047004b32b14fdfebecaec6db6075f485c6cd4c2191" :answer/id #uuid "e39dc574-480b-57d5-99b8-fd769235cb07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{12}},\\,0,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{12}}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33136/selection/6615875bc5df8d069e0a40217d368af0520aaa77afe0cd96eba8c2cfdd1a493d" :answer/id #uuid "0b8f1921-7e69-575d-9872-5ca8b7b3cd4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{2},\\,0,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33136/selection/0be08e9486ae03ab665b2d8e7b267dfe3f5c2b73d4e27ddac49d92e711d75dda" :answer/id #uuid "6b18d4b5-1c0a-5832-9020-771152a05bc8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{12}},\\,0,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{12}}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33136/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "eb6615ec-89c0-5f31-b71b-be380265d7c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-33136/selection/6615875bc5df8d069e0a40217d368af0520aaa77afe0cd96eba8c2cfdd1a493d" :answer-field/choices ["q-33136/selection/e8d6feaa001eb3c9330fa1ba584495e0468f420576d60f79541ab81caf1ae026" "q-33136/selection/f91e2a7ff49a9f08d8794e2ce1312cf01e9f082d710055202362908d714e9a41" "q-33136/selection/a7aad54674d1bdc909be7047004b32b14fdfebecaec6db6075f485c6cd4c2191" "q-33136/selection/6615875bc5df8d069e0a40217d368af0520aaa77afe0cd96eba8c2cfdd1a493d" "q-33136/selection/0be08e9486ae03ab665b2d8e7b267dfe3f5c2b73d4e27ddac49d92e711d75dda"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-33136" :question/id #uuid "f9509fd3-fbb9-5924-93c0-2012029b0bc2" :question/math-academy-id "q-33136" :question/problem "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{t}^{2}⟩$ at the point where $t=\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "For a curve $r(t)=⟨x(t),y(t),z(t)⟩$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=\\pi :$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot 2t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\sqrt{3}t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(\\pi ) & =⟨\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ,\\,\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,\\,\\sqrt{3}\\pi ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\pi ,\\,0,\\,\\sqrt{3}\\pi ⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(\\pi ):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖ & =\\sqrt{(-\\pi )^{2}+(0)^{2}+(\\sqrt{3}\\pi )^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{\\pi }^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(\\pi )$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at the point where $t=\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\pi ) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(\\pi )}{‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }⟨-\\pi ,\\,0,\\,\\sqrt{3}\\pi ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{2},\\,0,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-33136/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ff1822c-afad-54f8-aa36-7e0de79d9d04"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-33136"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-33584/selection/49b3ac5580d63fe44a690b973aaf26fa6bf6481f09191a3997ec52340ff270b3" :answer/id #uuid "3593da56-4529-5477-8995-4d5dfea4bf6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33584/selection/079aa508d06345e62a87203a9b7cc8fc49e9294d84f440723c32518faf7d18d6" :answer/id #uuid "c3a6d6fc-9abd-5b11-9c4e-756f1ac99a06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,i+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,j+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33584/selection/9e684b3ed0bad95a63ccc1d6fdf39eaee0aad75ab59ee847e2c5366e43a57fc5" :answer/id #uuid "3d3cf64b-53c5-5601-9bf2-57e7b73a12ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,i-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33584/selection/5f2c51777b5bb31703db80adbc8384e28b6740b21c40d31618ef1cf408e743e5" :answer/id #uuid "5183eaa4-7c6b-5c51-9da4-706cc8d3f980" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,j+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33584/selection/26ac17b1a3e5632fdf044a6dc6c939bd97b3f9d9ed53e305ffce8baa526f9c11" :answer/id #uuid "57ebf62e-a5e2-5fe0-9ee2-57a47167f5f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\,i+\\frac{2}{3}\\,j+\\frac{1}{3}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33584/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7c156753-5ae3-5a89-86d7-afe1d181da84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-33584/selection/26ac17b1a3e5632fdf044a6dc6c939bd97b3f9d9ed53e305ffce8baa526f9c11" :answer-field/choices ["q-33584/selection/49b3ac5580d63fe44a690b973aaf26fa6bf6481f09191a3997ec52340ff270b3" "q-33584/selection/079aa508d06345e62a87203a9b7cc8fc49e9294d84f440723c32518faf7d18d6" "q-33584/selection/9e684b3ed0bad95a63ccc1d6fdf39eaee0aad75ab59ee847e2c5366e43a57fc5" "q-33584/selection/5f2c51777b5bb31703db80adbc8384e28b6740b21c40d31618ef1cf408e743e5" "q-33584/selection/26ac17b1a3e5632fdf044a6dc6c939bd97b3f9d9ed53e305ffce8baa526f9c11"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-33584" :question/id #uuid "93a1c03f-77b3-5fa3-b1a1-22418386cc31" :question/math-academy-id "q-33584" :question/problem "What is the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=2t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j+t\\,k$ at the point $P(2,1,1)?$" :question/worked-solution "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)\\,j+y(t)\\,j+z(t)\\,k$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by \n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(2,1,1)$ on the given curve. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =2\\,i+\\,j+\\,k \\\\ 2t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j+t\\,k & =2\\,i+\\,j+\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the respective components gives the system\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2t=2 \\\\ {t}^{2}=1 \\\\ t=1.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equality, $t=1.$ This value satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, the point $P(2,1,1)$ is at the tip of $r(1).$ \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=1:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,i+2t\\,j+\\,k \\\\ {r}^{′}(1) & =2\\,i+2(1)\\,j+\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,i+2\\,j+\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(1)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at $P(2,1,1):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(1)}{‖{r}^{′}(1)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(2\\,i+2\\,j+\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\,i+\\frac{2}{3}\\,j+\\frac{1}{3}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-33584/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ff1822c-afad-54f8-aa36-7e0de79d9d04"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-33584"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-33581/selection/cfc7b15c863480fd079c2bce7119c081d3252fce3fe7f66338189217645c40aa" :answer/id #uuid "00c26a91-1af0-51b3-920d-98f4f03aad45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{3},\\,-\\frac{2}{3},\\,-\\frac{2}{3}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33581/selection/395e3ff9ca09acefa2b3f3fff65a15c37ed2d0ea399115fab79bb292709ce24a" :answer/id #uuid "06240440-75af-5208-8f78-3ee1310d6cad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3},\\,-\\frac{2}{3}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33581/selection/207f3c4f6d25b37441ab09fc6da896c1bb533e888fc3a797ef164dc6ecee7572" :answer/id #uuid "d9a9a058-e3d0-5240-b445-c732948d3f3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33581/selection/c5e2d1a8777e2dccad2a4fd3d56e759b5f76b9524a035dc3f7c96f17efe89459" :answer/id #uuid "91ee61ea-a20d-5059-9b92-ba7ffe53b375" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3},\\,-\\frac{2}{3}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33581/selection/98e3f8b58d891956304d0ce169e0488d14bc1b9eaed6fc3d330bc344b690ed50" :answer/id #uuid "df5254c9-c6e3-5f4b-8859-48682d0832af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{3},\\,-\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33581/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b10303ea-b772-5d16-b46b-60f1902d6da7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-33581/selection/cfc7b15c863480fd079c2bce7119c081d3252fce3fe7f66338189217645c40aa" :answer-field/choices ["q-33581/selection/cfc7b15c863480fd079c2bce7119c081d3252fce3fe7f66338189217645c40aa" "q-33581/selection/395e3ff9ca09acefa2b3f3fff65a15c37ed2d0ea399115fab79bb292709ce24a" "q-33581/selection/207f3c4f6d25b37441ab09fc6da896c1bb533e888fc3a797ef164dc6ecee7572" "q-33581/selection/c5e2d1a8777e2dccad2a4fd3d56e759b5f76b9524a035dc3f7c96f17efe89459" "q-33581/selection/98e3f8b58d891956304d0ce169e0488d14bc1b9eaed6fc3d330bc344b690ed50"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-33581" :question/id #uuid "92796ab5-2384-5790-88fb-e5402cb18b2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-33581" :question/problem "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩$ at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a curve $r(t)=⟨x(t),y(t),z(t)⟩$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,-2,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})‖ & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{‖{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨-1,\\,-2,\\,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{3},\\,-\\frac{2}{3},\\,-\\frac{2}{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-33581/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ff1822c-afad-54f8-aa36-7e0de79d9d04"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-33581"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127297/selection/9d659bb30df8142443010656adbb4e9ee9deb7f541987ebe4d0931158328fee1" :answer/id #uuid "42e7e92f-dc48-5770-8eb8-a1edbb928bec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}\\,j+\\frac{2}{5}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127297/selection/8272f78411633aa1e000587c5211d42ab3ac98b2a16e2f81e245f2fa548fa2a5" :answer/id #uuid "f6b53e29-33f7-5070-a372-f36fb7275984" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{10}\\,i-\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{10}\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127297/selection/3167cdf793ebd247d70422d1a694646edb9bc18280a1112b654c6f229f456f24" :answer/id #uuid "005f0765-63a2-50d2-bbe1-50f9e5d7a1bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}\\,j+\\frac{4}{5}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127297/selection/8cf1064fd7523cf26069da867d4ba2ecf631c2f43824379308d18e94e6d2011d" :answer/id #uuid "1b123334-9c4a-5c87-8c78-f19b6e5fa00c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}\\,i-\\frac{3}{5}\\,j+\\frac{4}{5}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127297/selection/d34ba915ea58f72b31456759fe5f7f3dc7a08cb4d5e1cbe22039de14c78b291f" :answer/id #uuid "7ab4ae83-b502-5d3c-b4c8-091a6249e48b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}\\,i-\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{10}\\,j+\\frac{4}{5}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127297/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6bda6acc-eec9-5a37-9b89-8325c1e7f99b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127297/selection/3167cdf793ebd247d70422d1a694646edb9bc18280a1112b654c6f229f456f24" :answer-field/choices ["q-127297/selection/9d659bb30df8142443010656adbb4e9ee9deb7f541987ebe4d0931158328fee1" "q-127297/selection/8272f78411633aa1e000587c5211d42ab3ac98b2a16e2f81e245f2fa548fa2a5" "q-127297/selection/3167cdf793ebd247d70422d1a694646edb9bc18280a1112b654c6f229f456f24" "q-127297/selection/8cf1064fd7523cf26069da867d4ba2ecf631c2f43824379308d18e94e6d2011d" "q-127297/selection/d34ba915ea58f72b31456759fe5f7f3dc7a08cb4d5e1cbe22039de14c78b291f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127297" :question/id #uuid "0198acc1-2b82-5c3b-8465-7072caeaf3ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-127297" :question/problem "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=(t+{t}^{3})p(t)$ at the point where $t=1$, if $p(1)=\\,i-2\\,j+k$ and ${p}^{′}(1)=-2\\,i+\\,j+2\\,k.$" :question/worked-solution "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j+z(t)k$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((t+{t}^{3})p(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+{t}^{3})p(t)+(t+{t}^{3})\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(p(t)) \\\\  & =(1+3{t}^{2})p(t)+(t+{t}^{3}){p}^{′}(t) \\\\ {r}^{′}(1) & =(1+3(1)^{2})p(1)+(1+{1}^{3}){p}^{′}(1) \\\\  & =4(i-2\\,j+k)+2(-2\\,i+\\,j+2\\,k) \\\\  & =-6j+8\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-6)^{2}+(8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36+64} \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(1)}{‖{r}^{′}(1)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}(-6\\,j+8\\,k) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}\\,j+\\frac{4}{5}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit tangent vector to the curve at the point that corresponds to $t=1$ is $T(1)=-\\frac{3}{5}\\,j+\\frac{4}{5}\\,k.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-127297/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "34342124-8cee-5b70-bf57-64f746af8912"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127297"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127298/selection/014e70dc7fedd07cbc050d87e78a240e1e976af1ccbd84d1a84d87e3d30c0dcd" :answer/id #uuid "cd0b3c5a-1251-5b6d-aa5d-9341112cef46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\,i-\\frac{2}{3}\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127298/selection/a466833195a30a366504720075c8de0d27ae0df8ce32db3740822850fa6b23c9" :answer/id #uuid "368ce218-610d-549a-80b0-27c1edaa6a53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\,i+\\frac{2}{3}\\,j-\\frac{1}{3}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127298/selection/a7346551a60e95059f7d462e18931e2dc143222484d318a99dcd8ea67925d70b" :answer/id #uuid "a8c7387d-7d20-5807-bf02-dce7fbdd4d6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}\\,j-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127298/selection/6eddebbe3077592d2373428b6b482691ea55568114d6b5b368921156322357d5" :answer/id #uuid "29dd2064-a074-5db9-b318-a615db2afcf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\,i-\\frac{2}{3}\\,j-\\frac{2}{3}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127298/selection/c406497b0f238af774f4e5bb6fec241960675e52a908218da7a2eeefb9325b5f" :answer/id #uuid "7ae531c1-b7ad-5d0d-b17e-35ce976dae0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\,i-\\frac{2}{3}\\,j-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127298/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bf96b916-5ec0-50cd-984f-d06fcf02331c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127298/selection/6eddebbe3077592d2373428b6b482691ea55568114d6b5b368921156322357d5" :answer-field/choices ["q-127298/selection/014e70dc7fedd07cbc050d87e78a240e1e976af1ccbd84d1a84d87e3d30c0dcd" "q-127298/selection/a466833195a30a366504720075c8de0d27ae0df8ce32db3740822850fa6b23c9" "q-127298/selection/a7346551a60e95059f7d462e18931e2dc143222484d318a99dcd8ea67925d70b" "q-127298/selection/6eddebbe3077592d2373428b6b482691ea55568114d6b5b368921156322357d5" "q-127298/selection/c406497b0f238af774f4e5bb6fec241960675e52a908218da7a2eeefb9325b5f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127298" :question/id #uuid "b5b234d3-95b5-5e8d-a6f9-df8675102205" :question/math-academy-id "q-127298" :question/problem "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+1}\\,p(t)$ at the point corresponding to $t=0$, given that  $p(0)=2\\,i+j-k\\,$ and $\\,{p}^{′}(0)=i-2\\,j-2\\,k.$" :question/worked-solution "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j+z(t)k$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=0:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+1}\\,p(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+1})\\cdot p(t)+\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+1}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(p(t)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2t}{{({t}^{2}+1)}^{2}}\\,p(t)+\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+1}\\,{p}^{′}(t) \\\\ {r}^{′}(0) & =-\\frac{2(0)}{{({0}^{2}+1)}^{2}}\\,p(0)+\\frac{1}{{0}^{2}+1}\\,{p}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =0(2\\,i+j-k)+(\\,i-2\\,j-2k) \\\\  & =\\,i-2\\,j-2k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(0):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖r(0)‖ & =\\sqrt{(1)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(0):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(0) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(0)}{‖{r}^{′}(0)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (i-2\\,j-2\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\,i-\\frac{2}{3}\\,j-\\frac{2}{3}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit tangent vector to the curve at the point that corresponds to $t=0$ is  $T(0)=\\frac{1}{3}\\,i-\\frac{2}{3}\\,j-\\frac{2}{3}\\,k.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-127298/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "34342124-8cee-5b70-bf57-64f746af8912"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127298"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-75141/selection/657114e84f56e91abfa66dcc65a002b863c6e6e0954199d00e11cf7c40a7816b" :answer/id #uuid "0ba54814-9804-5efe-affe-9a1bb275f269" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}\\,i+\\frac{4}{5}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75141/selection/e02e03b96cf3d4c987fc22fc5fa348fdc06f12b188ca0823e62277d70aefb323" :answer/id #uuid "ec346467-17eb-532a-a551-6e542c592a3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,i+\\frac{1}{2}\\,j+\\frac{1}{2}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75141/selection/59ef0fd6ca9c7a46113022ae2ddbcece3a20c136fe6eb23da2785a38e7408356" :answer/id #uuid "6f865317-1304-5216-b706-d86fdc39ae8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{5}\\,i+\\frac{1}{5}\\,j+\\frac{4}{5}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75141/selection/f5e4bf19445b540ebc114d71fb566863071c0e826eecab3b877c25774c30f6f3" :answer/id #uuid "a8f4d562-6d07-5763-8455-91c5cf0bd4c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75141/selection/cc64ba0df851842de4858416b92e274034ed45873ff9b722b6ed97a7033e537e" :answer/id #uuid "aee82325-7cf1-5db9-a2b6-2443b1998aa6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}\\,j+\\frac{2}{5}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75141/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e5b4f5a3-df25-555a-b870-800afaa4693e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75141/selection/657114e84f56e91abfa66dcc65a002b863c6e6e0954199d00e11cf7c40a7816b" :answer-field/choices ["q-75141/selection/657114e84f56e91abfa66dcc65a002b863c6e6e0954199d00e11cf7c40a7816b" "q-75141/selection/e02e03b96cf3d4c987fc22fc5fa348fdc06f12b188ca0823e62277d70aefb323" "q-75141/selection/59ef0fd6ca9c7a46113022ae2ddbcece3a20c136fe6eb23da2785a38e7408356" "q-75141/selection/f5e4bf19445b540ebc114d71fb566863071c0e826eecab3b877c25774c30f6f3" "q-75141/selection/cc64ba0df851842de4858416b92e274034ed45873ff9b722b6ed97a7033e537e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75141" :question/id #uuid "3ed1058b-f95e-52ec-88a0-53cf7dfda702" :question/math-academy-id "q-75141" :question/problem "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)={t}^{3}p(t)$ at the point corresponding to $t=1$, given that  $p(1)=-2\\,i+\\,j+\\,k\\,$ and $\\,{p}^{′}(1)=3\\,i-3\\,j+\\,k.$" :question/worked-solution "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j+z(t)k$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=1:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}p(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})\\cdot p(t)+{t}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(p(t)) \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}\\,p(t)+{t}^{3}\\,{p}^{′}(t) \\\\ {r}^{′}(1) & =3(1)^{2}\\,p(1)+(1)^{3}\\,{p}^{′}(1) \\\\  & =3(-2\\,i+\\,j+\\,k)+(3\\,i-3\\,j+\\,k) \\\\  & =-6\\,i+3\\,j+3k+3\\,i-3\\,j+\\,k \\\\  & =-3\\,i+4\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(1):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖r(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(0)^{2}+(4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(1):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(1)}{‖{r}^{′}(1)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (-3\\,i+4\\,k) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}\\,i+\\frac{4}{5}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit tangent vector to the curve at the point that corresponds to $t=1$ is  $T(1)=-\\frac{3}{5}\\,i+\\frac{4}{5}\\,k.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-75141/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "34342124-8cee-5b70-bf57-64f746af8912"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75141"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-33096"] :question/problem "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)={e}^{-t}p(t)$ at the point where $t=0$, if $p(0)=\\,i+\\,j+k$ and ${p}^{′}(0)=\\,i-\\,j.$" :question/worked-solution "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j+z(t)k$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t}p(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t})p(t)+{e}^{-t}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(p(t)) \\\\  & =-{e}^{-t}p(t)+{e}^{-t}{p}^{′}(t) \\\\ {r}^{′}(0) & =-{e}^{0}p(0)+{e}^{0}{p}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =-(\\,i+\\,j+k)+(\\,i-\\,j) \\\\  & =-2j-k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(0)‖ & =\\sqrt{(0)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+4+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(0) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(0)}{‖{r}^{′}(0)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}(-2j-k) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}j-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit tangent vector to the curve at the point that corresponds to $t=0$ is $T(0)=-\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}j-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}k.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-127280/selection/c617aeb25389021d18b4d5b8c27b6778a846404b263e4c1d57ab580cfa913ce2" :answer/id #uuid "ed930ade-b3b3-59f7-9c9f-34dfdf78761b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\,i-\\frac{2}{3}\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127280/selection/c8a1bbdd1fdcfa9aea1f1750bbec61d73d3b617752d731dd5276638c61fedd92" :answer/id #uuid "b7b5be51-9a99-5757-a6e1-2f837806d4cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{15}\\,i-\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{15}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127280/selection/6d0ba8c3a087df87da3d3692a619e7e99d5c9441ff1827e8b36c6f037add925f" :answer/id #uuid "53ffaa6f-94e7-5cac-b5e6-6a16b91278f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\,j-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127280/selection/4a3553284413dccc40e05a587d56369abe9968bc6030d07b2b2d95fcbd8525ae" :answer/id #uuid "0c81fa8a-44df-5ef8-8cc1-6b3c109b778a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\,i-\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127280/selection/93a6e9f81de33bdaceacffb6d7e99c643b22ed9ec52e38111279457a194814cb" :answer/id #uuid "1f3c99a8-51d0-5e8e-b30d-5d4100c941b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}\\,i-\\frac{4}{15}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127280/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4c1aebd0-6630-5db6-9502-2bc923b44600" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127280/selection/c8a1bbdd1fdcfa9aea1f1750bbec61d73d3b617752d731dd5276638c61fedd92" :answer-field/choices ["q-127280/selection/c617aeb25389021d18b4d5b8c27b6778a846404b263e4c1d57ab580cfa913ce2" "q-127280/selection/c8a1bbdd1fdcfa9aea1f1750bbec61d73d3b617752d731dd5276638c61fedd92" "q-127280/selection/6d0ba8c3a087df87da3d3692a619e7e99d5c9441ff1827e8b36c6f037add925f" "q-127280/selection/4a3553284413dccc40e05a587d56369abe9968bc6030d07b2b2d95fcbd8525ae" "q-127280/selection/93a6e9f81de33bdaceacffb6d7e99c643b22ed9ec52e38111279457a194814cb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127280" :question/id #uuid "d723ae58-372c-51a5-a554-97e4efb7ff33" :question/math-academy-id "q-127280" :question/problem "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,p(t)$ at the point corresponding to $t=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}$, given that  $p(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\sqrt{3}\\,i+\\sqrt{3}\\,k$ and $\\,{p}^{′}(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=-2\\,i-8\\,j+4\\,k.$" :question/worked-solution "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j+z(t)k$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,p(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\cdot p(t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(p(t)) \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,p(t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,{p}^{′}(t) \\\\ {r}^{′}(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{3})p(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{3}){p}^{′}(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}(\\sqrt{3}\\,i+\\sqrt{3}\\,k)+\\frac{1}{2}(-2\\,i-8\\,j+4\\,k) \\\\  & =(3\\,i+3\\,k)+(-\\,i-4\\,j+2\\,k) \\\\  & =2\\,i-4\\,j+5\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})‖ & =\\sqrt{(2)^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{45} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})}{‖{r}^{′}(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{5}}\\cdot (2\\,i-4\\,j+5\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{15}\\,i-\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{15}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit tangent vector to the curve at the point that corresponds to $t=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ is\n $T(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{15}\\,i-\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{15}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\,k.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-127280/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "34342124-8cee-5b70-bf57-64f746af8912"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127280"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3055"] :question/problem "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $\\mathbf r(t)=\\left\\langle \\sin^3{t}, \\:\\cos^3{t} \\right\\rangle$ at an arbitrary point where $0 < t < \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a curve $\\mathbf r(t)= x(t) \\,\\mathbf i + y(t) \\,\\mathbf j,$ the unit tangent vector $\\mathbf T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t))$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\mathbf T(t)=\\dfrac{\\mathbf r'(t)}{\\left\\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\right\\|}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $\\mathbf r(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({sin}^{3}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({cos}^{3}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3{cos}^{2}⁡t(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of $\\mathbf r'(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =|3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t|\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\ \\text{ } & =|3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t|\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =|3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t|\\sqrt{1} \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the last step, we were able to remove the absolute value bars because $\\sin{t}>0$ and $\\cos{t}>0$ for $0 < t < \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}.$\n\nFinally, we normalize $\\mathbf r'(t)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩}{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3054"] :question/problem "What is the unit tangent vector to the curve ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/1a5a0925f4e15e00c9eff4bb4f39ce9c6eda232881bbddb07184ac54bbc269a8.png) at the point ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/1e24125540d8b43cf8d314684fef6fb5be15c62d6988f9aac984f9812e6a74fd.png)" :question/worked-solution "For a curve ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/d7ec57597ee1ec3ed5d675c6d1cfde0115309f037e92d4aae963be1e54c97173.png) the unit tangent vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/beaa6501c934b5c7325c3b3385bae9fcc0388a74d5983995c83f4d8813e93f06.png) at the point ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/5313a9faaa4dde443c2eb79dedc7d917f6640579d0f038ffaf045ed01fd465f4.png) is given by \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/ff0324d951fb404b12736c08195532ce8d2fe57cae5baf845673b3626b871eb6.png) \n\nFirst, we find the value of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/7a5dc70352bd991ad75358cc62cef8d67afbb5cb00da1578f008a0b392d2385d.png) that corresponds to the point ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/83fbafba1d5d5be0d132254724f1cadcd31c51dc923c63113d0f393bf6bf94bc.png) on the given curve. We know that\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/aebba9c47fe0ea053b4fc1924e7f3a97ee17dc60fc074091ba0f6c303301cfda.png)\nIn the above equation, the first component in each of the two vectors is equal to ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/549c2a20cf7ec79cb4b26e39d950105c670a74452b2d7d024d3d5e64d553ecbe.png) Equating the other two components gives the system\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/187d4f3cd4d27fdac888ccf0d88c58f0cfb073913999f5767584476d9d2d4e10.png)\nFrom the first equation, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/02ad803439ddfa163c4788fb00ff86c65d3e0dc0711af87290695a8f06471e81.png) This value satisfies the second equation too. Therefore, the point ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/3d4f13f8fb24239874d83180ba75954be6d86ec8bb6e339bea3a0c1c9a4edae4.png) is at the tip of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/7479ebb2b1c8ed8146f6833341d2e732dcd91f86781823d36906dd19cadca82c.png) \n\nNow, we calculate ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/2a03e92cf496f1508de5344917e1f5fe5574f9801a0ef229649288a29c15044b.png) and evaluate it at ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/06f646a39990b7ed47b7ab431b54ea320a05650e5e4f6df6f51812460536154b.png)\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/9432511f61bf63030d95771cdc107682a61444fe925dab681ab8388b4a48524e.png) \n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/3b10ec5094240cfd7f221bc22e19a29d74b4a69d2788887265041cc7db5291ca.png)\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/ff9d6534ce414a2151a6dbbe2d407328ed6514447608f8601dfed6a1de27471c.png)\n\nFinally, we normalize ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/e9ece600ee31f7dc6e24c0639da455b0bba4fc3a7765986b08473109a93f0883.png) and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/5deae1091d1cd3c2502da1214919e0520c8cbe620d0ae3c2f1f926caf52f3cc0.png)\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/f110fc18608eb66b7f1927adb60049b76390669485638da4cddd592e23738998.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3056"] :question/problem "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $\\mathbf r(t)=e^{2t}\\mathbf p(t)$ at the point where $t=0,$ if $\\mathbf p(0)=\\mathbf i-\\,\\mathbf j-\\mathbf k$ and $\\mathbf p'(0)=\\mathbf i - \\mathbf j+ 2\\mathbf k.$" :question/worked-solution "For a curve $\\mathbf r(t)=x(t)\\mathbf i+y(t)\\mathbf j+z(t)\\mathbf k,$ the unit tangent vector $\\mathbf T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf T(t)=\\dfrac{\\mathbf r'(t)}{\\left\\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\right\\|}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $\\mathbf r'(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2t}p(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2t})p(t)+{e}^{2t}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(p(t)) \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t}p(t)+{e}^{2t}{p}^{′}(t) \\\\ {r}^{′}(0) & =2{e}^{2(0)}p(0)+{e}^{2(0)}{p}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =2(i-\\,j-k)+1(i-j+2k) \\\\  & =3\\,i-3\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of $\\mathbf r'(0)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(0)‖ & =\\sqrt{(3)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+(0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2\\cdot {3}^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize $\\mathbf r'(0)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(0) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(0)}{‖{r}^{′}(0)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}(3\\,i-3\\,j) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(i-j) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(i-j)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit tangent vector to the curve at the point that corresponds to $t=0$ is $\\mathbf T(0) = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\mathbf i -  \\mathbf j).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
